ggml-cpu flash attention: align prefill chunks to Q tiles (upstream PR #30921, open)

From https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30921 ("ggml-cpu : align flash attention prefill chunks to q tiles").
The tiled kernel always computes whole 64-row Q tiles; chunks that cut a tile make several threads compute the same
tile. With 6 threads, 512 rows and 16 heads, about 15% of the tile work at depth 1,100 was repeated (derived).
Upstream measured +3.5% to +25.8% on x86. Drop this patch when the PR is merged and the pin moves past it.

